Lander II
=========

An enhanced, Zarch-like game grown from David Braben's Lander, the
1987 demonstration game that came with the first Archimedes computers
and grew into Zarch. It is written in JavaScript, and all of it is in
this application directory for you to read and change.

Double-click !Lander2 to play. It takes over the whole screen (or opens
a window: see Display below) and leaves its icon on the icon bar; click
the icon to play again.

Flying
------
The mouse flies the ship, as in Lander. Imagine the pointer in the
middle of the screen: there the ship sits level. Move the mouse away
from the middle and the ship tilts that way - the further, the more.
The pointer is hidden and captured while you play (click once if it
isn't), so press C to put it back in the middle if you lose track.

  Select (left)      thrust        Space or Z
  Menu (middle)      hover         X or Shift
  Adjust (right)     fire          Return or Ctrl
  -                  dip / raise   Up / Down (or W / S)
  -                  rotate        Left / Right (or A / D)
  -                  missile       M
  -                  smart bomb    B
  -                  re-centre     C
  -                  pause         P
  -                  menu, back    Escape

The engine pushes out of the top of the ship: tilt a little and thrust
in short bursts. Land gently on the grey launch pad to refuel. A
gamepad works too: the left stick tilts, A thrusts, X fires, B hovers,
Y fires a missile, LB a smart bomb and Start pauses.

The games
---------
Invasion   Waves of aliens spray a red virus over the land. Shoot them
           before it spreads: seeders, drones (which can turn into
           mutants), bombers, pests, fighters and attractors. Clean
           land at the end of a wave scores a bonus. Every shot costs
           a point; there is an extra ship, missile and smart bomb
           every 5000 points.
Lander+    The original game on the original landscape: 20 points for
           each tree or building you shoot, -1 a shot, rocks falling
           from the sky once you pass 800 points.

Left alone, the title page plays a demo game, flown by the Autopilot.

Settings
--------
Look (Enhanced, or Classic: 320 x 256 as the Archimedes drew it), view
distance, resolution, full screen or window, sound (Original, Arcade or
off) and volume, controls, mouse speed, difficulty (Zarch plays by the
authentic rules: no hover), game speed, particles, shadows, stars and
fog. F (or Browser in Settings) uses the whole computer screen.

Display: the icon bar menu also switches between Full screen and
Window; the window can be resized.

The settings are kept in Choices:Lander2.Settings and the high scores
(one table for each game) in Choices:Lander2.Scores - JSON text files in
$.!Boot.Choices.Lander2 that you can read in !Edit. Delete Scores to
start the tables again.

The source
----------
Choose View source on the title page or the icon bar menu to read the
program in !JsEdit, or Open directory to see the files. Shift-double-
click a file to open it in !JsEdit. !RunImage starts it all; World and
its helpers are the game, Render draws it, Sound makes the noises, and
Hud, Screens and Play are what you see. Change something, save, and
run !Lander2 again to try it.

Lander is (C) D.J.Braben 1987; the formulas come from Mark Moxon's
commentary on its source at https://lander.bbcelite.com. The original
program itself is !Lander, next to this one in Diversions.
